/* The strings iOS renders on the app's behalf: the Home-screen name and the permission sheets.
 *
 * These are NOT in Localizable.strings and cannot be — the system reads them out of the bundle
 * before the app runs, which is why a missing key here is a hard crash the first time the API is
 * called rather than a label that says its own name. The English values in `Info.plist` exist so the
 * key is present at all; these are what a passenger actually reads.
 */

/* Transliterated rather than translated, and deliberately (C076's call, kept). This is the consumer
 * app: its icon sits on a home screen beside apps labelled in Sinhala, and AL-26's whole point is
 * that a Sinhala-first passenger is not handed an English product. The driver app needed no such
 * decision because its name carries a translatable noun. */
"CFBundleDisplayName" = "MageRide";

"NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "Your location centres the live map, shows the vehicles within about 3 km of you, and fills in your pickup point.";
